From 3b61801bba161c59009c7d47097fcec27d4cd0d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mboot <mboot@deb-gui-usa.rl.lan>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:37:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rosco_m68k: sigreturn restores the condition codes

do_sigreturn() took the whole status register from the process at the
sigreturn call, so the interrupted code went on with the signal handler's
condition codes: a signal between a compare and its branch changed the
branch.  On the M68000 the user byte (X N Z V C) now comes from the
sigcontext; the supervisor byte stays protected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ROSCO_M68K_CONVERSATION_LOG.md | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/kernel/system.c            |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ROSCO_M68K_CONVERSATION_LOG.md b/ROSCO_M68K_CONVERSATION_LOG.md
index b159db6..12ad9c5 100644
--- a/ROSCO_M68K_CONVERSATION_LOG.md
+++ b/ROSCO_M68K_CONVERSATION_LOG.md
@@ -1478,3 +1478,26 @@ Not committed yet.
   * MAME (CONSBAUD=115200): PF1, then Escape in a running
     `REPEAT ... UNTIL FALSE`, gives "Escape at line 10".
 * Rebuilt: the default `boot/image.bin` (38400).
+
+## sigreturn keeps the condition codes (2026-10-21)
+
+* **Problem** (found by the BBC BASIC port, whose ESCape is now a SIGINT
+  from the console):
+  * `do_sigreturn()` (system.c) restored every register from the
+    sigcontext except the status register. It took that from the process
+    as it was at the sigreturn call (`sc.sc_psw = rp->p_reg.psw`, there
+    so that a user cannot set supervisor bits).
+  * So the interrupted code resumed with the condition codes of the
+    signal handler's exit, not its own. A signal between a compare and
+    its branch changed where the branch went.
+  * BBC BASIC failed about one run in four (Syntax error, lost state); C
+    code compiled by ACK or gcc is exposed to it the same way.
+* **Fix (M68000):** the supervisor byte stays as it is; the user's X N Z
+  V C come from the sigcontext:
+  `sc.sc_psw = (rp->p_reg.psw & ~0x1F) | (sc.sc_psw & 0x1F)`.
+* **Tested** with the port's terminal test (ESCape signals during loops,
+  GET, INKEY with *ESC OFF, after *commands): 20 of 20 runs pass, against
+  about 3 of 4 before.
+* **Rebuilt:**
+  * the default `boot/image.bin` (38400);
+  * the MAME image (CONSBAUD=115200) in the BBCZ80 tree.
diff --git a/src/kernel/system.c b/src/kernel/system.c
index 6b9e99d..4fdc383 100644
--- a/src/kernel/system.c
+++ b/src/kernel/system.c
@@ -655,7 +655,15 @@ register message *m_ptr;
 	rp->p_reg.sp = sc.sc_sp;
 	return (OK);
   }
+#if (CHIP == M68000)
+  /* The supervisor byte stays as it is, but the condition codes (X N Z V
+   * C) are the interrupted code's: a signal between a compare and its
+   * branch must not change where the branch goes.
+   */
+  sc.sc_psw  = (rp->p_reg.psw & ~0x1F) | (sc.sc_psw & 0x1F);
+#else
   sc.sc_psw  = rp->p_reg.psw;
+#endif
 
 #if (CHIP == INTEL)
   /* Don't panic kernel if user gave bad selectors. */
-- 
